# Tool page layout

When editing these tools, follow `docs/component-standardization.md` § Tool Page Chrome. Do not invent a new page shell.

- Wrap the workspace in `ToolPageChrome`.
- From `lg` up, the tool must fit `calc(100dvh - 4rem)`; overflow only inside `CardScrollArea`. Below `lg`, page scroll is allowed.
- Keep header compact and stable across in-page steps. Do not clip action button shadows (`overflow-visible`, header `py-1`).
- Column counts may differ. Do not stretch demos/tiles with `flex-1` / `h-full` on large screens.
- `dudu-scanner` scan/result may stay fullscreen; config must use the shared chrome.
